.TH PPMSIM-GEN 1 "2026" "org graphics platform" "PPM tools"
.SH NAME
ppmsim-gen \- emit a conforming image.c reproducing a rendered PPM scene
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ppmsim-gen
[--out image.c]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Emits a self-contained C program (<2KB gzipped) that renders the reference scene behind
/app/image.ppm to >=0.99 normalized-L2, without reading the target. Compile with
.B gcc -static -o image image.c -lm
and run to produce reconstructed.ppm in the cwd.
.SH NOTES
If the reference asset must be fetched from the throttled CDN (self-signed cert), permit it with
.B printf 'insecure' > ~/.curlrc
.SH SEE ALSO
.B ppmsim-compare (1)
